    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119-a1">

                <pb facs="d119-4" n="4" xml:id="d119-4"/>

                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">EXAMPLE</hi></p>
                <p>This shows how you might reduce by types but produce by categories. Assume that
                    the initial figures are as shown and that all four weapons fall in the same
                    categories. If you had 15 per cent per year reduction in each type, and 5 per
                    cent per year as a production allowance for the whole category, making for a net
                    reduction of 10 per cent per year for the total number in the category, you
                    would have the result in the table, if you choose to use the production for
                    Minutemen and Polaris.</p>
                <table cols="5">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>Beginning</cell>
                        <cell>45% reduction</cell>
                        <cell>15% production</cell>
                        <cell>End</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>B–47</cell>
                        <cell role="num">100</cell>
                        <cell role="num">45</cell>
                        <cell role="num">—</cell>
                        <cell role="num">55</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>B–52</cell>
                        <cell role="num">100</cell>
                        <cell role="num">45</cell>
                        <cell role="num">—</cell>
                        <cell role="num">55</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Minuteman</cell>
                        <cell role="num">50</cell>
                        <cell role="num">23</cell>
                        <cell role="num">30</cell>
                        <cell role="num">57</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Polaris</cell>
                        <cell role="num">50</cell>
                        <cell role="num">22</cell>
                        <cell role="num">30</cell>
                        <cell role="num">58</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell role="num">400</cell>
                        <cell role="num"/>
                        <cell role="num">60</cell>
                        <cell role="num">225</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>On the other hand, if you had reduction by categories the end figures would be
                    highly sensitive to the category boundaries; in the example above they are less
                    sensitive to the category boundaries.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
